<title>USA: Sherwin-Williams unit buys Brazilian firm.</title>
<headline>Sherwin-Williams unit buys Brazilian firm.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sherwin-Williams Co said on Monday its Brazilian subsidiary bought Sumare Industria Quimica SA for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Sumare makes industrial maintenance and chemical-coating products, with a plant near Sao Paulo. Its annual sales, translated into U.S. dollars, are about $35 million.</p>
<p>The Sherwin-Williams subsidiary involved in the transaction is Sherwin-Williams do Brasil Industria e Comercio Ltda.</p>
</text>
